-### Training Ray Sub-sampling
-Training Ray Sub-sampling is a dataset transform that sub-samples a fixed number of rays from a multiview batch for training or rendering [S11, unofficial]. It generates random ray indices using `torch.randint`, sub-samples rays and ray values (channels) using these indices, and returns contiguous tensors [S11, unofficial].
+### [Training Ray Sub-sampling](13130-training-ray-sub-sampling.md)
+Training Ray Sub-sampling is a data transform that reduces the number of rays processed per training iteration by selecting a fixed subset from a larger batch of multiview rays. It solves the problem of high memory consumption and computational cost during radiance-field optimization by limiting the batch size to a manageable `num_samples` count. Unlike [Batch Ray Sampling](2767-batch-ray-sampling.md), which determines *which* rays enter the pipeline, this method determines *how many* of those rays are actually forwarded to the network for gradient computation.
 
